section('architecture','System architecture','1:00',`<div class="section-top"><span class="eyebrow">10 / HOW THE SYSTEM CONNECTS</span><span class="section-number">10</span></div><h2>Two interfaces.<br><em>One communication backbone.</em></h2><div class="architecture"><div class="architecture-end"><span>RESIDENTS</span><h3>Flutter Android</h3><p>Information access<br>Concern submission<br>Community tools</p></div><div class="architecture-core"><span>SHARED BACKEND</span><h3>Firebase</h3><div class="backend-labels"><span>Authentication</span><span>Firestore</span><span>Storage</span><span>Cloud Functions</span><span>Notifications / FCM</span></div></div><div class="architecture-end"><span>AUTHORIZED STAFF</span><h3>Web dashboard</h3><p>Targeted publishing<br>Scoped case handling<br>Operational records</p></div></div><p class="architecture-note">Local quick answers and a cloud-assisted route support assistant guidance. Weather information uses Open-Meteo.</p><div class="scope-row"><h3>Access follows responsibility.</h3><p>The system distinguishes resident access and assigned barangay, department, organization, and administrative roles.</p></div>`,'light-section')+
section('evaluation','Evaluation & boundaries','0:55',`<div class="section-top"><span class="eyebrow">11 / RESEARCH EVIDENCE</span><span class="section-number">11</span></div><div class="research-split"><h2>Demonstrate the work.<br><em>Measure the outcome.</em></h2><div><p class="lead">The evaluation chapter will bring together actual workflow tests and the study’s user-evaluation findings.</p><p class="small-note">Evaluation results have not yet been supplied. This section keeps space for verified evidence without inventing scores or participant counts.</p></div></div><div class="evaluation-grid"><div><span>01</span><h3>Functionality</h3><p>Submission, publishing, replies, status, and notifications.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Usability</h3><p>The study’s actual procedure, participants, and findings.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Access & audience</h3><p>Role boundaries and communication to intended recipients.</p></div></div><div class="boundaries"><h3>Scope to explain in the defense</h3><p>Emergency communication supports information and coordination. Saved announcements support specific offline access. Market listings connect people. The assistant guides access to existing tools.</p></div>`)+
section('research','The thesis & discussion','1:00',`<div class="closing"><span class="eyebrow">12 / E-SUGID</span><h2>A connected community.<br><em>A conversation worth having.</em></h2><p class="thesis-title">E-sugid: Design and Development of a Centralized Community Communication and Information Dissemination System</p><div class="closing-actions"><button class="primary" data-start-defense>Restart the defense</button><a class="text-button" href="#staff">Explore the staff dashboard</a></div><p class="discussion-label">QUESTIONS & DISCUSSION</p><details class="research-details"><summary>Read the complete proposed objectives</summary><ol><li>Define community information, publishing, feedback, and staff communication requirements.</li><li>Design the Android, staff web, and shared-backend architecture and interfaces.</li><li>Develop centralized official announcements, safety notices, and intended-audience information access.</li><li>Implement resident concerns and follow-up, with private complaints as a separate workflow.</li><li>Implement verification and role-based, scoped administration.</li><li>Provide community information tools and assistant guidance within their defined scope.</li><li>Evaluate functionality, usability, intended-audience communication, and role access using the actual study procedures.</li></ol><p>Proposed content grounded in the application and supplied title. Confirm against the approved manuscript. Team, institution, adviser, final methods, and evaluation findings are still to be supplied.</p></details></div>`);
